<title>CHINA: China's Guangxi 1996 grain output seen at record.</title>
<headline>China's Guangxi 1996 grain output seen at record.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guangxi province in south China is expected to produce a record of 15.9 million tonnes of grain in 1996, the People's Daily newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>The province's agricultural output was forecast to total 90.7 billion yuan ($10.9 billion) in 1996, a rise of nine percent from 1995, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Natural disasters had trimmed fruit output slightly it said but production of other agricultural products was up. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
</text>
